{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>From the ground.</b> Rashi's interpretation: more than it was already cursed in its season — that is, because it did not produce a tree whose taste and the taste of its fruit were the same. Another interpretation: <b>cursed are you from the ground</b> — on account of the ground. How so? When you work the ground in this year, it will no longer give you its strength in another year; therefore you shall immediately be a fugitive and a wanderer, and find yourself cursed." "<b>Which opened its mouth to receive your brother's blood.</b> And the blood corrupts the earth; therefore when you work the ground it will no longer give you its strength and its produce, as long as you and your seed are in the world. Therefore you shall be a fugitive and a wanderer, pursuing your sustenance in the land, as it is written: נודד ללחם איה."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:55.286316852Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}